<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    updatePeriodMillis is intentionally 0: Android's built-in widget update period is
    unreliable and has a 30-minute floor, so refresh scheduling is done entirely with our own
    WorkManager job (WidgetScheduler), as recommended for Glance widgets.

    widgetCategory includes keyguard (in addition to home_screen) so TipWidget is eligible for
    lock-screen/communal-hub widget pickers, not just the home screen — without it, the OS
    filters this widget out of that picker before the app is ever involved.

    On the sizes: a tip is up to ~90 characters of 15sp serif, and the card spends chrome on
    padding, the quote glyph and the app-name label before drawing any of it. The old
    140x90dp minimum could not fit that on either axis — ~12 characters per line against a
    6-line cap, with the chrome alone exceeding the declared height — which is what made long
    tips clip. Width is the cheaper axis to buy: a wide, short card fits a tip in few lines,
    so the default is 4 cells wide by 2 tall (250x110dp on the standard 70n-30 grid).

    minResize* stays lower than min*: the launcher lets a user shrink the widget below the
    default, and TipWidget's SizeMode.Responsive has a compact layout (no quote glyph, no
    footer, 12sp) built for exactly that. It is a real fallback, not an accident.

    targetCellWidth/Height are API 31+ and draw two expected `UnusedAttribute` lint warnings
    against minSdk 26. They are kept anyway: on 31+ they let the launcher place the widget by
    grid cells directly, and on 26-30 they are ignored in favour of minWidth/minHeight above,
    which describe the same shape. Both are needed to cover the whole range.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:minWidth="250dp"
    android:minHeight="110dp"
    android:minResizeWidth="180dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="110dp"
    android:targetCellWidth="4"
    android:targetCellHeight="2"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="0"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen|keyguard"
    android:previewImage="@mipmap/ic_launcher"
    android:description="@string/widget_description" />
